\\in A$ implies $x\\in B$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f2500b511dd686a64c6f4145"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A = \\{1,2\\}$ and $B = \\{2,3\\}$. What is $A\\cup B$?","options":["$\\{2\\}$","$\\{1,2,3\\}$","$\\{1,3\\}$","$\\{1,2,2,3\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fe67c226d240539d82de31f5"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_004","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which identity is the distributive law of union over intersection?","options":["$A\\cup(B\\cap C)=(A\\cup B)\\cap(A\\cup C)$","$A\\cup(B\\cap C)=A\\cup B\\cup C$","$A\\cup(B\\cap C)=(A\\cap B)\\cup C$","$A\\cup(B\\cap C)=A\\cap B\\cap C$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"415ce3c78af88b5c6cdbe6f4"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement expresses commutativity of union?","options":["$A\\cup(B\\cup C) = (A\\cup B)\\cup C$","$A\\cup B = B\\cup A$","$A\\cup\\varnothing = A$","$A\\cup B = A$ for all sets $A$ and $B$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3109bad4a1c99a41d0a51927"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement expresses associativity of union?","options":["$A\\cup B = B\\cup A$","$A\\cup(B\\cup C) = (A\\cup B)\\cup C$","$A\\cup\\varnothing = A$","$A\\cup A = \\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"051de8a874b659004269ee0b"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $x\\in A$ and $x\\notin B$, what can be concluded about $x$ and $A\\cup B$?","options":["$x\\notin A\\cup B$","$x\\in A\\cup B$ only if $B$ is empty","$x\\in A\\cup B$","$x\\in A\\cup B$ only if $x$ also belongs to $B$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"caa6ef6cacda4a9300c949cc"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A = \\{1,4\\}$, $B = \\{4,5\\}$ and $C = \\{5,6\\}$. What is $A\\cup(B\\cup C)$?","options":["$\\{4,5\\}$","$\\{1,6\\}$","$\\{1,4,4,5,5,6\\}$","$\\{1,4,5,6\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9efdb8b1361c1643ea312f8e"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement best captures the boundary case involving the empty set?","options":["$A\\cup\\varnothing = \\varnothing$ for every set $A$.","$A\\cup\\varnothing$ contains only elements not in $A$.","$A\\cup\\varnothing$ is undefined unless $A$ is finite.","$A\\cup\\varnothing = A$ for every set $A$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5ef40a7f711dea2e9a4759eb"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is the condition '$x\\in A$ or $x\\in B$ or both' important for $A\\cup B$?","options":["Because common elements are excluded from the union.","Because an element must occur twice to be in the union, in all instances without exception.","Because elements common to both sets are included, but still appear as elements of one set.","Because union only applies to disjoint sets."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b0636ff9e8a68e77b02d581e"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A\\cup B = \\{1,2,3\\}$ and suppose $A = \\{1,2\\}$. What set can $B$ be?","options":["$\\{4\\}$","$\\varnothing$","$\\{2,3\\}$","$\\{1,2,4\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1898c3c8ae4d5a199e78af0e"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_union_of_sets_0ba36bc3_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $A\\cup B = A$, which conclusion is forced by the definition of union?","options":["Every element of $A$ is already an element of $B$.","Every element of $B$ is already an element of $A$.","$A$ must be the empty set.","$B$ must contain no elements of $A$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fa96050a0566a659a3e8f471"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How does $A$ relate to $A\\cup B$ as sets?","options":["$A\\subseteq A\\cup B$","$A\\cup B\\subseteq A$","$A=A\\cup B$ for all $B$","$A$ and $A\\cup B$ are disjoint"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ee6895bb98c9295ab40e55a4"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_014","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For finite sets $A$ and $B$, what does $|A\\cup B|$ equal?","options":["$|A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|$","$|A|+|B|$","$|A|\\cdot|B|$","$|A|-|B|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"557e83a29cffece2a3ca2759"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_015","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"When does $A\\cup B=A\\cap B$ hold?","options":["Exactly when $A=B$","For all sets $A,B$","Only when both are empty","Never"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7d12287d80d4755fa44829f5"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $|A|=3$, $|B|=4$, and $|A\\cap B|=1$, what is $|A\\cup B|$?","options":["$6$","$7$","$8$","$5$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bea59f703d98dc3e21a35ec8"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_017","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $A$ and $B$ are disjoint finite sets, what is $|A\\cup B|$?","options":["$|A|+|B|$","$|A|\\cdot|B|$","$0$","$|A|-|B|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d138931334c9804019837521"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\{1,2\\}\\cup\\{1,2\\}$?","options":["$\\{1,2\\}$","$\\{1,1,2,2\\}$","$\\varnothing$","$\\{1\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"de2f027c9eab0627dd69489a"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_019","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How does union differ from intersection?","options":["Union uses 'and', while intersection uses 'or'.","Union uses 'or', while intersection uses 'and'.","Union excludes elements in both sets.","Union is defined only for empty sets."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"07e45ec89288ce9934185359"},{"id":"union_of_sets_new_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $A\\subseteq B$, what is $A\\cup B$?","options":["$A$","$\\varnothing$","$B$","$A\\cap B$ is undefined"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"91d7cb91895a673863ccf3db"}]}}